          "reasoning": "On workstation5.corp.local, powershell.exe (proc-8b801b5203) running as CORP\\pgustavo made 10 outbound connections to 10.10.10.5:80 starting at 04:18:48 on 2020-07-22. That is the likely C2 server. At 04:19:04 it wrote a base64/UTF-16 PowerShell stager into HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Debug. When decoded, the stager matches PowerShell Empire: it turns off script-block logging through cachedGroupPolicySettings. The same process then added a Run value named 'Updater' under HKLM\\...\\CurrentVersion\\Run. At startup it reads the Debug value and runs it with 'powershell -Win Hidden -enc', so the C2 stager comes back after every reboot. The process also created a registry key (reg-d91a9c1c29), which I did not inspect, so it needs checking. Verdict: malicious, fileless registry persistence plus C2.",
